# Linux File Management & Archiving Essentials

A comprehensive reference guide covering fundamental Linux command-line tools for file manipulation, organization, and archiving. This repository serves as a practical handbook for professional system administration tasks.

## 📌 Core Command Overview

| Command | Purpose | Common Use Case |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `mkdir` | Create directories | Setting up new project folder structures |
| `mv` | Move or rename files | Organizing assets or renaming logs |
| `cp` | Copy files and folders | Backing up configuration files before editing |
| `rm` | Remove files or directories | Cleaning up temporary build artifacts |
| `tar` | Tape Archive utility | Bundling and compressing large datasets |
| `ls` | List directory contents | Inspecting files, structures, and metadata |

